  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A ripple baby blanket is a 75 x 90 cm flat rectangle with a shallow zigzag running across its width, worked back and forth in one piece on a foundation chain. The wave is made by working a five-treble shell at each peak and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " twice at each valley, so the stitch count stays constant across every row."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK cotton in two or three colours is the classic choice: each colour runs for two rows to make clean stripe edges. At this gauge the blanket fits a standard cot lengthways with 10 cm overhang. Total yardage is around 350 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton, Colour A (main)",
              "qty": "150 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "DK cotton, Colour B",
              "qty": "100 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "DK cotton, Colour C",
              "qty": "100 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "16 dc x 9 rows = 10 x 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook. Gauge matters here because the ripple pattern is balanced on a multiple of 12 stitches plus 3. A one-stitch difference per 10 cm shifts the finished width by about 5 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc (UK) / sc (US): double crochet, the valley stitch"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "tr (UK) / dc (US): treble, five into the same stitch make the peak shell"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc2tog (UK) / sc2tog (US): double crochet two together, the valley decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation chain"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using Colour A, chain 123. This sets up 10 ripple repeats (12 stitches each) plus 3 edge stitches."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1 (right side)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "turning-chain"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "turning chain"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of ch 1 (does not count as stitch). Dc into 2nd ch from hook. Dc into next ch. *Skip 2 ch. Work 5 tr into next ch (peak shell made). Skip 2 ch. Dc into each of the next 3 ch. Then dc2tog over next 2 ch, dc2tog over next 2 ch (valley made). Dc into each of next 3 ch*. Repeat to last 6 ch. Skip 2 ch. Work 5 tr into next ch. Skip 2 ch. Dc into last 3 ch. Turn. (10 peaks, 9 valleys, flat ends.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 (wrong side)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 1. Dc into first stitch. *Dc into each of next 2 stitches. Work 5 tr into the 3rd tr of peak. Dc into each of next 2 stitches. Dc2tog twice (valley). Dc into each of next 2 stitches*. Repeat. End with 5 tr into last peak, dc into last 3 stitches. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stripe sequence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 2 rows each in Colour A, Colour B, Colour C, back to A. Continue until piece measures 90 cm. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join Colour A at any corner. Work one round of dc around the entire border, working 1 dc into each stitch along top and bottom, 1 dc into each row end on sides, and 3 dc into each corner. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to secure each tail along 3-4 stitches in matching colour rows. Block lightly with a steam iron held 2 cm above the surface to relax the ripple."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 30 degrees gentle. Dry flat. The ripple stretches in width when wet, so pin to the stated width while drying if the blanket is for a cot."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chevron blanket uses the same ripple base but with a sharper peak. Or try the corner-to-corner baby blanket for a diagonal take on the same stitch count."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}